      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "I need to search for recent Toronto Maple Leafs news to provide current context for this column, given that their season has ended.\n\nLet me search for the latest developments.\n\n---\n\nThe rebuild clock is ticking in Toronto, and the silence is deafening. <strong>The Maple Leafs' season ended in a seven-game tailspin</strong> - a 32-36-14 record, eighth place in the Atlantic, 31 points behind the division leader - and now the hard questions arrive: Did Auston Matthews and Mitch Marner carry a roster too thin to compete? Did the goaltending betray them? Did the system fail? The answers will determine whether this franchise pivots toward contention or another lottery year. At 78 points and 15th in playoff positioning, Toronto didn't just miss the postseason - they watched it from home while Buffalo and Montreal battled in Round Two. The front office faces a summer of reckoning: coaching staff changes, cap flexibility decisions, and whether this core can still win together. <strong>The draft lottery awaits, and so does the accountability tour.</strong> This organization has promised contention for a decade. That promise is now a debt.",
        "updated": "Updated May 10, 2026"
      },
