        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "# The Morning Skate: Lay of the Land\n\nDan Quinn didn't come to Washington to rebuild from a 5-12 cellar. He came to fix it. <strong>The Commanders' rookie class just inked their contracts, and first-round linebacker Sonny Styles - already drawing comparisons to veteran Bobby Wagner around the league - signals the team's commitment to a defensive reset.</strong> Last year's wreckage sits three games behind the division lead, and Quinn made clear he won't hide behind injury excuses. That's not the language of a man content with triage.\n\nThe draft haul tells the story: Styles anchors a linebacker corps that bled yards a season ago. The secondary got attention too - safety was flagged as a critical need, and the front office moved accordingly. Rachaad White arrives in the backfield from Tampa Bay, a veteran anchor for the rushing attack. None of this screams \"we're tanking.\" It screams \"we're building around what works and burying what doesn't.\"\n\n<strong>The real test arrives in August, when these rookies face their first NFL speed.</strong> Styles will be tested immediately. The margin for error is razor-thin. Quinn knows it.",
